// probes/data/font-blob.kdl -- a font read out of a `data` node.
//
// A font node that names `data` is embedded, and doc/printout.md#data
// lists embedded fonts among the entries of the header's `data` table.
// Its entry is named as an image's is: the font table's `resolvedData`
// names it, and it is written because the font is used.
//
// - `small` and `large` read `one` and `two`, which hold the same bytes,
//   so they share one entry.  `large` is the first font an element is
//   built in, so the entry takes the name of the node it reads, `two`,
//   and both fonts' `resolvedData` say so;
// - `unused` reads `three`, and no element is built in it:
//   it is not in the font table, and `three` is not written.
//
// The face is Go Regular cut down to `x`, `y` and its `.notdef`,
// so that the recorded answer stays readable.  The two sizes keep
// the two fonts apart; two font nodes the same in everything but
// their names are the question printout/twin-fonts asks.

report name="data/font-blob" {
  font "small" data="one" size=10
  font "large" data="two" size=12
  font "unused" data="three" size=10
  data "one" encoding="base64" {
    content """
      AAEAAAAKAIAAAwAgT1MvMkTXSW4AAAEoAAAAYGNtYXAADADMAAABlAAAADRnbHlm
